# POP Audit Platform — Complete Technical Handover, Current State, Requirements, and Implementation Roadmap

## 1. Role and Mission

Act as a senior DevOps engineer, network automation engineer, Python backend developer, Docker specialist, and ISP/NOC systems architect.

I am developing an application called **POP Audit**, a Site Health Check Platform for an Internet Service Provider.

The goal is to provide a professional NOC web application in which an operator enters only a Site Code, and the platform automatically discovers the devices belonging to that POP, checks their health, analyzes radio links, displays the results, and generates downloadable reports.

This is an existing project. Continue from its current implementation rather than rebuilding it from scratch.

Your priorities are:

1. Preserve all currently working functionality.
2. Fix the remaining discovery and monitoring issues.
3. Complete the unified radio table, twelve-hour historical analysis, NCS discovery, and switch log display.
4. Complete Docker Compose containerization.
5. Verify the complete system using real monitoring data.
6. Improve reliability and security without disrupting the existing host.

**Do not claim anything is complete until it has been verified against the actual code, running service, and real API responses.**

---

# 2. Main Project Information

Project name:

```text
POP Audit
```

Primary server directory:

```text
/opt/pop-audit/
```

Main configuration file:

```text
/opt/pop-audit/config/.env
```

Python virtual environments:

```text
/opt/pop-audit/venvs/
```

Current project directories:

```text
/opt/pop-audit/
├── config/
├── gateway/
├── orchestrator/
├── zabbix-service/
├── cisco-service/
├── ericsson-service/
├── radio-service/
├── report-service/
├── reports/
├── logs/
├── shared/
├── sql/
└── venvs/
```

The established microservice architecture uses seven services.

| Service | Source directory | Native port | Responsibility |
|---|---|---:|---|
| Gateway | `/opt/pop-audit/gateway/` | 8000 | Web UI and public-facing API |
| Orchestrator | `/opt/pop-audit/orchestrator/` | 8001 | Async jobs and service coordination |
| Zabbix Service | `/opt/pop-audit/zabbix-service/` | 8002 | Site/device discovery and monitoring data |
| Cisco Service | `/opt/pop-audit/cisco-service/` | 8003 | Cisco switch SSH checks |
| Ericsson Service | `/opt/pop-audit/ericsson-service/` | 8004 | Ericsson checks using Moshell |
| Radio Service | `/opt/pop-audit/radio-service/` | 8005 | RTN/EBand and other radio link analysis |
| Report Service | `/opt/pop-audit/report-service/` | 8006 | Excel report generation and download |

The native systemd services are:

```text
pop-audit-gateway.service
pop-audit-orchestrator.service
pop-audit-zabbix.service
pop-audit-cisco.service
pop-audit-ericsson.service
pop-audit-radio.service
pop-audit-report.service
```

Native Python environments use Python 3.12.

The current application is written primarily in Python using FastAPI, with HTTP communication between the microservices.

The frontend uses HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript.

