# 6. Zabbix Service

Location:

```text
/opt/pop-audit/zabbix-service/
```

Main files:

```text
/opt/pop-audit/zabbix-service/app/main.py
/opt/pop-audit/zabbix-service/app/client.py
/opt/pop-audit/zabbix-service/app/discovery.py
/opt/pop-audit/zabbix-service/app/metric_models.py
/opt/pop-audit/zabbix-service/app/models.py
/opt/pop-audit/zabbix-service/app/radio_metrics.py
```

Port:

```text
8002
```

The service exposes discovery functionality through its API. The main discovery endpoint used by the Orchestrator is:

```text
POST /discover
```

The service is responsible for discovering:

- Basebands/eNodeBs.
- Cisco switches.
- NCS Cisco devices where applicable.
- Outgoing RTN links.
- EBand links.
- Other supported radio link types.

The service also retrieves monitoring metrics, history, and trigger information used by the radio analysis.

A previous bug was fixed: retrieving triggers for a host must authenticate the Zabbix API client first.

The correct sequence includes:

```python
client.login()
```

before calling the trigger retrieval method.

Do not regress this behavior.

## Discovery requirements

The current discovery logic needs to be reviewed carefully.

Inspect:

```text
/opt/pop-audit/zabbix-service/app/discovery.py
```

Determine why the second baseband is missing.

Check whether:

- The initial host search finds all applicable hosts.
- Group filters remove valid hosts.
- Site Code matching is too restrictive.
- Hostname parsing assumes only one baseband.
- A result is being overwritten instead of appended.
- The Orchestrator drops additional discovered records.
- The frontend or report exporter assumes a single device.

Fix the root cause. Do not create a special case that works only for one Site Code.

