# 7. Cisco Service

Location:

```text
/opt/pop-audit/cisco-service/app/main.py
```

Port:

```text
8003
```

The Cisco service uses SSH with Netmiko/Paramiko.

The following commands have been used by the established implementation:

```text
show version
show inventory
show interfaces status
show interfaces description
show interfaces
show logging
show environment
show env temperature status
show environment status
show environment summary
```

Existing checks include:

- Device identity/version.
- Inventory.
- Interface status and descriptions.
- Interface operational/admin state.
- CRC errors.
- Input errors.
- Output errors and drops.
- Logging.
- Environment checks.

Established behavior includes:

```text
CONNECTED / UP       → PASS
disabled             → PASS
err-disabled         → PASS
suspended            → PASS
inactive             → PASS
NOTCONNECT / DOWN    → WARNING
CRC > 0              → WARNING
errors > 0           → WARNING
```

Generic speed-mismatch rules were deliberately avoided because some switches legitimately operate at different negotiated speeds.

Do not add a new speed rule without a verified operational requirement.

## Verified Site 2488 Cisco result

```text
STATUS      PASS
INTERFACES  PASS
LOGGING     PASS
ENV         PASS
```

## New requirement: NCS switch discovery

Some POPs have two associated Cisco switches.

The normal switch includes the Site Code in the hostname.

Example:

```text
TH-BH-SW-2225-SaadatAbad
```

The second switch is an NCS device.

Example:

```text
TH-BH-RTR-NCS-SaadatAbad-Agg
```

The NCS hostname does not necessarily include the Site Code.

Known NCS patterns:

```text
TH-BH-NCS
```

```text
TH-BH-RTR-NCS
```

The application must discover the primary switch using the Site Code, then find and associate the applicable NCS switch using shared location information and other available metadata.

The association algorithm must not use a fixed mapping for Site `2225` alone.

It must support other POPs.

Use Zabbix host information and verified hostname patterns to match the NCS candidate to the appropriate POP. If a location match is ambiguous, do not silently associate a potentially wrong switch.

The full workflow must pass both switches into the Cisco check service, and both devices must appear in the web results and Excel report.

## New requirement: last ten switch logs

At the bottom of the web page, display the latest ten log entries from:

1. The normal Cisco switch.
2. The associated NCS switch, when present.

Use the existing SSH command execution mechanism and actual switch output.

Verify how `show logging` output is ordered and parsed.

Do not show ten arbitrary lines if they are not the latest events.

If fewer than ten events exist, show the events available.

If the device has no NCS counterpart, display an appropriate unavailable/not-applicable state without failing the whole audit.

If log retrieval fails, report the failure rather than inventing logs.

