Location:

```text
/opt/pop-audit/ericsson-service/app/main.py
```

Port:

```text
8004
```

The Ericsson service executes Moshell checks through SSH to the configured Moshell host.

The Moshell host is:

```text
172.20.10.28
```

The remote hostname was verified as:

```text
ran-moshell-01
```

The Moshell binary on that remote host is:

```text
/home/a.torkashvand/Moshell25F/moshell
```

The working session method is important.

Do not use:

```text
moshell -e -f
```

because it bypassed the working rc/user-variable configuration.

The successful session method is equivalent to:

```text
moshell 172.27.193.42
```

Use a single interactive Paramiko shell session.

The tested command sequence was:

```text
Start Moshell session
Wait

lt all
Wait

st cel
Wait

alt
Wait

get . clock
Wait

q
```

The production implementation already includes parsers and a real Moshell execution path.

Existing checks include:

- Managed element connectivity.
- Cell status.
- Alarm collection and severity mapping.
- Clock status.

## Verified Site 2488 Ericsson result

Nine cells were found.

All nine cells were:

```text
UNLOCKED
ENABLED
```

Clock result:

```text
radioClockState 6
RNT_TIME_LOCKED
```

Clock status is PASS.

Actual alarms included:

```text
C License Key File Fault
w License Usage Exceeds Capacity
m External Link Failure
```

The parser uses case-sensitive alarm mapping:

```python
if severity == "C":
    CRITICAL
elif severity == "M":
    MAJOR
elif severity == "m":
    MINOR
elif severity == "w":
    WARNING
else:
    UNKNOWN
```

The baseline result was:

```text
STATUS : CRITICAL
ALARMS : CRITICAL
TOTAL  : 3
CRIT   : 1
MAJOR  : 0
```

Do not alter the working Moshell approach unnecessarily.

