/opt/pop-audit/radio-service/app/radio_rules.py
```

Port:

```text
8005
```

The main analysis endpoint is:

```text
POST /analyze
```

The service handles outgoing radio links discovered from Zabbix.

Supported link types must include:

- RTN
- EBand
- NRay
- Intracom

## Existing verified EBand rules

Difference:

```text
< 7 dB → OK
>= 7 dB → Not OK
```

The user has described the threshold as difference below seven being acceptable and a problem at seven or above. Verify the actual existing rule implementation and apply the same defined threshold consistently.

RX power:

```text
RX < -45 dBm        → CRITICAL
-45 <= RX < -37     → WARNING
RX >= -37           → PASS
```

Capacity threshold in the current logic is approximately:

```text
2.2 Gbps
```

However, the user has now explicitly requested **removal of Capacity Health** from the result presentation and report.

Remove the Capacity Health feature from the relevant health calculation and UI/report fields if it is dedicated to this feature. Do not delete an unrelated capacity metric if another required function still uses it.

Modulation expectations must remain based on the existing verified radio rules. A known 5G RX modulation expectation is 256 in the current EBand implementation.

Do not invent additional TX modulation, SNIR, BBER, BBE, ESR, ES, or other thresholds without validating the actual data and configured rules.

Verified Site 2488 EBand results:

```text
Kurosh EBand → PASS
Zafar EBand  → PASS
```

## Existing RTN rules

The verified modulation rule is:

```text
modulation >= 13 → PASS
modulation < 13  → WARNING
```

Difference:

```text
difference < 7  → acceptable
difference >= 7 → problem
```

Existing traffic threshold values are around:

```text
350 Mbps / 410 Mbps
```

Existing packet-loss trigger levels include:

```text
5%
20%
80%
```

The exact interpretation of each rule must be validated against the actual code before modification.

RTN may contain several individual links/legs.

Do not replace the existing radio-analysis algorithms simply to make the frontend table easier to implement.

## Verified Site 2488 radio result

```text
Overall Radio Status: WARNING

RTN: WARNING
EBand Kurosh: PASS
EBand Zafar: PASS
```

The actual EBand links have previously returned real values for RX/TX, calloff, difference, modulation, capacity, and interface checks.

