```

## Excel sheets already implemented

The working report contains:

```text
Summary
Devices
Cisco
Ericsson
Ericsson Alarms
RTN
EBand
```

Earlier workbook validation confirmed that these sheets exist and that the Summary contained:

```text
Site Code        2488
Overall Status   CRITICAL
CISCO            PASS
ERICSSON         CRITICAL
RADIO            WARNING
```

A bug in the RTN report parser was fixed after a runtime error:

```text
AttributeError: 'str' object has no attribute 'get'
```

The original parser assumed that every modulation value was a dictionary.

The fix made it tolerate strings, dictionaries, and lists where appropriate.

After the fix, `create_workbook()` succeeded and returned:

```text
STATUS : CRITICAL
```

Do not undo this compatibility fix.

## Required Excel changes

The Excel report must remain consistent with the actual web results.

Required changes:

- Remove Capacity Health.
- Consolidate RTN, EBand, NRay, and Intracom into one `Links` worksheet/section.
- Display actual numeric RX/TX Difference and Modulation values.
- Preserve link-specific health evaluation internally.
- Include all discovered basebands.
- Include the normal Cisco switch.
- Include the NCS switch where it is correctly associated with the POP.
- Preserve the existing Summary and other useful detailed information.
- Do not fabricate unavailable metrics.

After modifications, generate and inspect a fresh workbook using the Report Service virtual environment.

The report must open successfully using OpenPyXL.

