## Dependency handling

The native virtual environments were inspected.

The services use Python 3.12.

Known dependencies include:

- FastAPI.
- Uvicorn.
- Pydantic.
- Requests.
- HTTPX.
- Python-dotenv.
- Netmiko.
- Paramiko.
- OpenPyXL.

Some services have additional transitive dependencies.

Requirements files were intended to be generated from the existing venvs using `pip freeze`.

Verify compatibility with the actual chosen base images before considering container builds final.

Do not perform unnecessary dependency upgrades.

## Compose networking requirements

The native environment uses internal URLs such as:

```text
http://127.0.0.1:8001
http://127.0.0.1:8002
http://127.0.0.1:8003
http://127.0.0.1:8004
http://127.0.0.1:8005
http://127.0.0.1:8006
```

Those defaults are not suitable for communication between separate containers.

Inside Compose, use service DNS names, for example:

```text
http://orchestrator:8001
http://zabbix-service:8002
http://cisco-service:8003
http://ericsson-service:8004
http://radio-service:8005
http://report-service:8006
```

Configure the container environment correctly.

Do not unintentionally change native behavior when moving to Compose.

## Security requirements for Docker

- Do not copy `.env` into image layers.
- Use a restrictive `.dockerignore`.
- Mount secrets only where necessary or inject needed variables.
- Do not print secrets when inspecting Compose.
- Do not expose internal service ports unnecessarily.
- Publish only the Gateway.
- Persist reports outside the container.
- Use sensible restart policies such as `unless-stopped`.
- Implement health checks but also perform functional tests.
- Preserve the existing native deployment until cutover is validated.

## Persistent report directory

The host directory is:

```text
/opt/pop-audit/reports/
```

The Report Service should keep using it as a persistent volume:

```yaml
volumes:
  - /opt/pop-audit/reports:/opt/pop-audit/reports
```

This ensures generated Excel reports survive container recreation.

## Moshell connectivity in Docker

The Ericsson service connects to the configured Moshell server at:

```text
172.20.10.28
```

Keep that integration working from inside the Ericsson container.

Do not attempt to copy the remote Moshell executable into the container unless inspection proves it is needed.

The existing design uses SSH to the separate Moshell host.

